296:inference over 9 rounds, with 30000 initial simulations, and 20000 added simulations in each round. Our results, including the percentage of valid summary statistics versus the number of simulations, and a posterior predictive sample, are provided in Figure 4. We also provide a pairwise marginal plot of our final posterior approximation in Figure 7 (Appendix E.2). In the final round, we achieved $81 \%$ valid summary statistics from the simulator (Figure 4c), superior to the percentage achieved by other methods for the same simulation budget. We also note that the obtained posterior produces samples which closely match the observed data (Figure 4a). In addition, the posterior marginals (Figure 7) are very similar to others previously reported in the literature (Deistler et al., 2022a; Glockler et al., 2022).
